<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish minister gives go-ahead to Xtra-vision deal.</title>
<headline>Irish minister gives go-ahead to Xtra-vision deal.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's Minister for Enterprise and Employment Richard Bruton on Thursday said the take-over of Xtra-vision by Block buster Entertainment (Irl) Ltd should be allowed to go-ahead.</p>
<p>Bruton said in a statement that he had accepted the unanimous conclusion of the Competition Authority that the acquisition of Xtra-vision should proceed.</p>
<p>The Competition Authorities report on the take-over is being published as required by legislation, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9775</p>
